;; Replay stream generated by scripts/capture-to-replay.py --quote
;; from a raw MOSES capture log (see experiments/memo-prototype/).
;;
;; Order and repetition are preserved exactly as captured -- NO
;; deduplication -- because repeated candidates are the cache-hit
;; signal the memo-prototype benchmark measures. Each atom carries
;; an explicit sequence index because `collapse`-ing a space does
;; not guarantee iteration order; the replay driver walks by index.
;;
;; QUOTED variant (variant P / zipform-nary only): each candidate
;; expr is wrapped `(quote <expr>)`. Unlike the plain .replay.metta
;; files (whose AND/OR/NOT are inert only because this standalone
;; prototype's DEFAULT ops table gives them zero clauses), variant
;; P's zipform/ops-nary.metta DOES give AND/OR/NOT real clauses, so
;; a bare literal `(AND ...)` occurrence written directly in a file
;; that (transitively) imports ops-nary.metta would compile as a
;; goal call at translation time (whole-file-prescan rule, see
;; zipform/rewriter-nary.metta's header / probes/probe-zip-quote-
;; unfired.metta). The `quote` wrapper is the verified fix (see
;; probes/probe-nary-quote-store-retrieve.metta): add-atom stores
;; the quote-wrapped atom verbatim (never evaluated), and the
;; driver retrieves it via a quote-destructuring match pattern,
;; `(match &replayStream (candidate $i (quote $e)) $e)`, which
;; binds $e to the raw INERT tree -- confirmed by that probe to
;; stay inert through let-destructure and through being passed as
;; a plain function argument (e.g. into rewriteTreeNaryCached),
;; only firing AND/OR/NOT when the evaluator's own per-row
;; zipWithN dispatch later calls them deliberately.

!(bind! &replayStream (new-space))
!(add-atom &replayStream (candidate 1 (quote A)))
!(add-atom &replayStream (candidate 2 (quote (NOT (A)))))
!(add-atom &replayStream (candidate 3 (quote B)))
!(add-atom &replayStream (candidate 4 (quote (NOT (B)))))
!(add-atom &replayStream (candidate 5 (quote C)))
!(add-atom &replayStream (candidate 6 (quote (NOT (C)))))
